The name of the game is NetHack (or just Hack) in which one can encounter
the Oracle (at Delphi) and recieve sage advice.  It is a computer game of
long standing in which you explore a graphically represented maze.

The pick-axe (one of the things you can find) is for digging holes in walls
(floors, statues, doors, and a few other things too... but mostly walls)
and the chrysknife (which does indeed originally come from Dune) is gained
by enchanting a "worm tooth" (taken from a dead giant worm)... it is a fairly
respectable weapon good for slicing up fairly respectable monsters.

The Oracle charges you for such advice (in Nethack anyway) though why a potion
of speed rather than the standard ungodly amounts of gold I do not know.

